<title>ITALY: Italy offers 36.5 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</title>
<headline>Italy offers 36.5 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian treasury said it was offering 36.5 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT), replacing 39.81 trillion lire of expiring paper.  </p>
<p>A Treasury statement said it would offer:</p>
<p>*10.5 trillion lire of three-month BOTs</p>
<p>*12.0 trillion lire of six-month paper</p>
<p>*14.0 trillion lire of one-year bills.</p>
<p>Subscriptions close at 1200 GMT on February 25.</p>
<p>The Treasury added that it would offer 4.0 trillion lire of two-year zero couponed certificates (CTZ) and 2.0 trillion lire of 18-month CTZ.</p>
<p>Subscriptions for both those sales also close at 1200 GMT, on February 25</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
